{
	"extractedAt": "2026-11-17",
	"source": "https://open-design.ai/pricing — plan caps, credit multipliers and concurrency; token rates and long-context tiers from https://amr-api.open-design.ai/api/v1/public/model-prices, fetched 2026-11-17 (verbatim body kept at docs/plan/opendesign/reference/od-model-prices.json), not from core/zen.json",
	"creditUnit": "1 credit = $1 of the plan's allowance; a model spends list-price dollars x its multiplier",
	"notes": [
		"Only the Go plan publishes a 5-hour cap; every plan publishes a monthly one.",
		"The 7-day window resets from the subscription start, not Monday — the store records no subscription, so oduse cuts it as a rolling 7 days and says so.",
		"plan-model credits are a second, published allowance with no local meter: the store names models, not which of them are plan models.",
		"Design Plan caps are per model class, not per plan: Go publishes $220/mo, $55/7d and $18/5h for DeepSeek V4.1 Flash Eco, and $120/mo, $30/7d and $10/5h for the original DeepSeek V4.1 Flash. A plan's own caps are its default set (the Eco one on Go, named by defaultCapLabel); capOverrides names the models that get a different set. Pro/Max publish one set, so they carry no override.",
		"Every row in this table currently carries rateSource: published — the price list covers all 46 models, so no seeded estimate remains today. Open Design still publishes no multiplier, so the multipliers here stay as they were.",
		"rateSource has three possible values and only one is authoritative: published means the token rates came from Open Design's own price list; estimate means a seeded stand-in used only where no rate is published (none remain today); an absent field means no provenance claim at all. No consumer may present an estimate or an unlabelled row as a published price.",
		"A model's id is the gateway's wire id — what `GET /v1/models` returns and what the store records on a turn — so a recorded id always keys a row. `catalogId` names the same model in core/zen.json where that catalogue spells it differently (a dot versus a dash); absent, the id is the same on both sides.",
		"The multiplier for Claude Haiku 5.5 is 2x here while the billing page reads 4x; that conflict is open, so the value is left as published.",
		"The 32 rows added from the price list carry multiplier 1: the caps reference (docs/plan/opendesign/reference/od-caps.json) publishes a multiplier only for the original 14 models.",
		"A longContext tier replaces all four rates for a turn whose fresh input exceeds inputTokensAbove; the whole turn is repriced, not only the excess. The price list states the threshold but not that convention, so it is the common one and is unverified against a real over-threshold bill."
	],
